      "writtenOn": "2018-01-22T14:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do we want to do if the underlying network does not exist? Is netd responsible for returning ENONET? Since the recent changes to NetworkController locking, you Should(TM) be able to access the NetworkController netId map safely from binder threads without incurring races.\n\n(That\u0027s the authoritative source for which netIds are currently plumbed through.)\n\nYou can also do this in a slightly more racy way by doing something like ConnectivityManager.getLinkProperties(network).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1196,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1196,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "40b4bf1534b39f3811b88fa23b68db66e445077a",
