    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58009faa_6ab66543",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/IpSecService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1197,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-22T14:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any failure indication if the local address is invalid, does not exist, or is assigned to a different network? (I\u0027m assuming not, since netd does not readily have this information).\n\nThe most important thing to do is ensure there are no leaks of unencrypted traffic.\n\nOther than that: if you use the getLinkProperties suggestion above you will have this information, though the information you get may be out of date. Assuming (as above) that the underlying operation silently succeeds if you specify a policy with a non-existent address, you could call getLinkProperties(underlyingNetwork) twice, once before and once after applying the configuration. Even that\u0027s racy though, since it incurs a handler loop delay. Use NetworkInterface to get the IP addresses, perhaps?\n\nFor now a TODO is fine, assuming there are no leaks (and perhaps even if there are).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1197,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1197,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "40b4bf1534b39f3811b88fa23b68db66e445077a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17097fd6_cad8b8fa",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/IpSecService.java",
